# UI Consistency, Beauty & Compact Data Display (Mandatory)

Every UI change must look like it belongs in this admin theme: modern, polished, compact, and useful. Do not invent a parallel design system.

## Source of Truth

1. Read `.agent` first.
2. Match the closest existing screen (prefer **Users** / **Roles** / **Organization** settings panels).
3. Reuse shared theme building blocks before writing custom markup.

## Required Theme Building Blocks

Prefer these existing pieces over one-off UI:

- Layout / chrome: `Breadcrumb`, `DefaultLayout` patterns, `panel`, sidebar nav
- Lists: `DataTableWithSidebar`, `CustomDataTable` / datatable helpers, column configs
- Detail: sidebar via `DataTableWithSidebar` + `*Detail.tsx` (dense sections, not sparse pages)
- Forms / dialogs: `GenericModal`, `components/form/*` (`FormInput`, `FormSelect`, `FormCombobox`, `FormTextarea`, `FormDatePicker`, `FormSwitch`, `FileUpload` / `ImageUpload`)
- Feedback: `Loader`, `sonner` toasts, `useConfirmDialog`, existing `btn btn-primary` / `btn` variants
- Theme tokens: `theme.config.tsx`, Tailwind `primary` / `secondary`, light + **dark:** variants

Buttons and actions must use project button classes (e.g. `btn btn-primary gap-2`), not random unstyled or third-party-only button skins unless the twin screen already does.

## Compact Data Table Rules (Important Data Only)

Tables are for **scanning**. Keep them dense and high-signal.

- Show only columns that help identify / decide: identity (name/title), key status, primary relation, one date, actions.
- Do **not** dump every model field into the table.
- Prefer short labels, tight widths, and compact cell renders (`font-medium` for the primary label).
- Format dates compactly (e.g. `MM/DD/YYYY` or `MMM DD, YYYY`) — avoid noisy timestamps in table cells unless time is critical.
- Status / type fields should use clear badges or concise text consistent with nearby screens.
- Keep action columns icon-based via existing datatable action types (`view` / `edit` / `delete`).
- Avoid huge empty columns, multi-line essay cells, and decorative-only columns.

## Detail Sidebar / Detail Panel Rules (Complete Useful Data)

Detail views are for **full understanding**. Show complete useful data in a compact layout.

- Fetch the full record (`getById`) and display **all user-relevant fields** (identity, contact, status, relations, permissions/roles, audit timestamps, IDs as secondary meta).
- Do **not** leave details as only name + created/updated — that is incomplete.
- Group fields into tight sections with small uppercase/muted labels and compact value text (mirror Roles detail density; improve on sparse Users detail when touching it).
- Use `space-y-3` / small gaps; avoid large empty whitespace and oversized headings.
- Support light and dark (`text-gray-900 dark:text-white`, muted `text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400`).
- Loading / empty / error states must use `Loader` or concise centered messages — never a blank dead panel.
- Relations should be readable (role names, permission chips/lists), not raw opaque JSON.

## Modern Look Without Breaking Consistency

- Keep visual language aligned with existing panels, tables, modals, and forms.
- Use subtle hover/transition only where twins already do; no flashy unrelated motion.
- Prefer clear hierarchy: page title/breadcrumb → compact toolbar actions → dense table → rich detail sidebar.
- Forms inside modals should be structured, labeled, and responsive; reuse form components.
- Do not introduce a new card grid, purple gradient theme, emoji-heavy UI, or unrelated component library patterns when theme components already fit.
- Do not redesign the whole product unless the user explicitly asks.

## Page Composition Checklist (CRUD list screens)

For each list resource page:

1. `Breadcrumb`
2. `DataTableWithSidebar` with compact **important** columns
3. Sidebar `*Detail` with **complete** useful fields, dense layout
4. `*Modal` + `*Form` using shared form components and theme buttons
5. Bulk actions / primary CTA styled like Users (`btn btn-primary`)

## Anti-Patterns (Forbidden)

- Custom page layouts that bypass `DataTableWithSidebar` for standard CRUD lists
- Tables with every DB column or details with almost no fields
- Inconsistent spacing, one-off color palettes, or mixed button styles on the same page
- Huge padding / sparse “marketing” whitespace inside admin detail sidebars
- Ignoring dark mode classes on new UI text/surfaces
- Building parallel form controls when `components/form/*` already covers the need

## Completion Bar

UI work is incomplete unless:

- It matches theme components and twin-screen patterns
- Table columns are compact and decision-useful
- Detail shows complete useful data in a dense modern layout
- Light/dark styling is respected
- `.agent` is updated when UI conventions or shared components change
